\documentclass[11pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}
\usepackage{graphicx}

\title{Latency Characteristics of the Serving Pipeline}
\author{Inference Infrastructure Group}
\date{}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Online inference stacks fail in the tail, not in the mean.
This note documents the serving pipeline deployed in the
north region and the measurements we used to characterise
its tail latency. Figure~\ref{fig:pipeline} summarises the
request path, and the measurements that follow refer back
to its stages. All experiments ran on the production
shadow cluster during a quiet window in February.

\input{sections/results}

\section{Related Systems}
The earlier serving stack routed requests through a central
broker, and its latency profile was dominated by broker
contention rather than by queueing at the model workers.
The current design removes the broker entirely, so the
comparison with the old measurements is only qualitative.
A full migration report is circulating separately.
\end{document}

